WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:10.470 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  britney spears is back  [Music]  dropping her first new song in six years  a duet with elton john  the world is collectively celebrating  britt's long-awaited return after the  pop princess released a remix of elton's  1971 hit tiny dancer called hold me  closer  [Music]  drew barrymore is one of many brit fans  geeking out over the drop it's the first  project britney's put out since her  13-year conservatorship ended we gotta  say we're thrilled for brit and the pop  star sounds like she never missed a beat  on the track  [Music]  elton opened up to the guardian about  his experience working with brit in the  studio telling the outlet it took some  convincing to get the singer to release  their studio record quote she's been  away so long there's a lot of fear there  because she's been betrayed so many  times we've been holding her hand  through the whole process reassuring her  that everything's gonna be all right i'd  be very fortunate enough to be given the  gift of being able to make music and  that is a hell of a gift to be given and  it's a gift britt says she doesn't take  for granted as an artist before the  song's released britney tweeted i'm  kinda overwhelmed  but she felt honored to collaborate with  the pop rock legend tweeting it's pretty  damn cool that i'm singing with one of  the most classic men of our time  [Music]  and seems like the feeling is mutual  elton saying he was ecstatic when  britney agreed to collaborate praising  her on instagram she truly is an icon  one of the all-time great pop stars and  i love her dearly as for how the new  song came together music producer andrew  watt told the guardian brick brought her  a game in her recording session and was  incredibly specific about what she  wanted to do with her vocals she's  unbelievable at layering her voice and  doubling which is one of the hardest  things to do  she really pushed herself vocally  [Music]  we'd say brit and elton just ended the  summer with a smash hit and here's to  hoping there's more britney music in the  works since she did say this i want to  be fearless like when i was younger and  not to be so scared and fearful i choose  happiness and joy today  i'm in the tub right now and i'm about  to go have the best day ever  [Music]  crazy  [Music]

